      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-19586",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/ad/ad085590f1f45ee83e71f6ad20d2785604a36c8b9b3792952e87bf08893a8674.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed between the curves $y = 2x^{2} - 4x$ and $y = 4x - 2x^{2}$, as shown in the picture. Given that cross-sections perpendicular to the $x$-axis are isosceles right triangles with the hypotenuse lying on the $xy$-plane, calculate the volume of the solid.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
    {
      ":db/id": 17592186106373,
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/type": {
                ":db/ident": ":answer.type/math"
              },
              ":answer/value": "\\displaystyle \\int_{-2}^{2}(-\\frac{1}{4}x^{2} + 1)dx",
