      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-50693",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/54/540fe87774f13d8bfe8a61e44a4c7b9d45024a1a9eb217414b8b0cc380196053.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the region enclosed between the curves $y =-0.25x^{2} + 1$ and $y = 0.25x^{2} - 1$, as shown in the picture. If cross-sections perpendicular to the $x$-axis are isosceles right triangles with the hypotenuse lying on the base, which of the following gives the volume of the solid?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
